5d946e3bbd6ad696be91ed3 (completed, exit 0, TestAssuranceRestoreCommittedLogsContext passed, 53 parsed events) adds the end state of the split. Its split_result events reproduce the partition outcome of the two earlier receipts (both sides leading in the same term with no cross-side entry at parsed index 48), and its split_healed event at parsed index 49 shows the cluster convergi [preview: 1807 characters omitted; see full record]\",\n    \"counterevidence_count\": 4,\n    \"limitation_count\": 4,\n    \"view\": \"preview\",\n    \"record\": {\n     \"path\": \"state.json\",\n     \"collection\": \"interpretations\",\n     \"id\": \"0893ffb5551d46aebc7c1f80a94c73ff-interpretation-0\"\n    }\n   },\n   \"view\": \"preview\",\n   \"record\": {\n    \"path\": \"state.json\",\n    \"collection\": \"investigations\",\n    \"id\": \"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-question-0\"\n   }\n  }\n ],\n \"knowledge\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n   \"statement\": \"NewRaft re-derives Raft's own configuration from configuration-carrying log entries only for indices above max(lastSnapshotIndex, lastApplied); the other writers of r.configurations are snapshot restore, snapshot install and the leader's own appendConfigurationEntry path, and nothing else repairs it.\",\n   \"conditions\": \"Startup reconstruction in NewRaft over a log store; lastApplied may already be advanced by restoreFromCommittedLogs or by a restored snapshot; configuration entries are identified by LogConfiguration or the deprecated peer entry types.\",\n   \"view\": \"preview\",\n   \"record\": {\n    \"path\": \"state.json\",\n    \"collection\": \"knowledge\",\n    \"id\": \"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-knowledge-0\"\n   }\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-knowledge-1\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n   \"statement\": \"restoreFromCommittedLogs reads the commit index from a CommitTrackingLogStore, clamps it to the last log index, sets the commit index and calls processLogs, which applies the committed prefix to the FSM and sets lastApplied to that commit index; this happens after snapshot restore and before NewRaft's configuration scan.\",\n   \"conditions\": \"Config.RestoreCommittedLogs enabled and the log store implements CommitTrackingLogStore; the tracked commit index is at least the index of a configuration entry stored in the log.\",\n   \"view\": \"preview\",\n   \"record\": {\n    \"path\": \"state.json\",\n    \"collection\": \"knowledge\",\n    \"id\": \"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-knowledge-1\"\n   }\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-knowledge-2\",\n   \"revision\": 3,\n   \"kind\": \"fact\",\n   \"statement\": \"The configuration a node holds decides its own participation and support arithmetic: runFollower declines to campaign when latestIndex is zero or the local ID has no vote in the latest configuration, a candidate needs quorumSize() votes of the latest configuration, and the leader's commitment is constructed from the latest configuration, so a stale or empty reconstruction directly changes which su [preview: 30 characters omitted; see full record]\",\n   \"conditions\": \"The configuration is the one reconstructed at startup or later written by a snapshot install or a configuration change; quorumSize and the commitment are computed from configurations.latest.\",\n   \"view\": \"preview\",\n   \"record\": {\n    \"path\": \"state.json\",\n    \"collection\": \"knowledge\",\n    \"id\": \"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-knowledge-2\"\n   }\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-knowledge-3\",\n   \"revision\": 3,\n   \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n   \"statement\": \"appendEntries processes configuration entries only for the entries it newly appends; entries already present at the same index and term are skipped, so ordinary replication from a healthy leader does not re-derive the configuration of a follower whose log already matches.\",\n   \"conditions\": \"Follower handling a normal AppendEntries whose entries are duplicates of its own log; entries that are in the leader's compacted prefix instead arrive as an InstallSnapshot, which rewrites both configurations from the snapshot metadata. The same index-and-term comparison decides log conflicts: receipt 2996ef7e45d946e3bbd6ad696be91ed3 shows two entries at the same index and term with different cont [preview: 80 characters omitted; see full record]\",\n   \"view\": \"preview\",\n   \"record\": {\n    \"path\": \"state.json\",\n    \"collection\": \"knowledge\",\n    \"id\": \"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-knowledge-3\"\n   }\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"4d96d7967e324d6a98cfef381c9cad6a-knowledge-1\",\n   \"revision\": 6,\n   \"kind\": \"fact\",\n   \"statement\": \"A restart with Config.Restor\n=== investigations count 1\n=== knowledge count 19\n=== experiments count 12\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
